            "heading": "About Tea & Tonic",
            "heading_size": "h0"
          }
        },
        "template--16192093028523__4837950c-eea4-410f-8595-647c4cb7d4f1-text-1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Tea and Tonic is a holistic health store located in Matakana Village, with a focus on <a href=\"https://teaandtonic.co.nz/blogs/journal/supporting-women-in-business-going-plastic-free\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">sustainability, supporting women in business </span></a>and the art of gifting. Founded by Monni Jansen in 2017, Tea and Tonic is often described as a calm and thoughtful sanctuary that delights and soothes the senses.<br/><br/>Designed by one of New Zealand’s leading Architectural designers , Fraser Horton, the Tea and Tonic flagship store emanates harmony and tranquility, with influences from eastern design. Showcasing natural materials, the store connects to the elements that flow outside, from the neighbouring river to the courtyard of cherry blossom trees.<br/><br/>Through her own journey to wellbeing, Monni realized that all healing starts with love - love for oneself, others, and the world around us - and that the health of people and our planet go hand in hand. This understanding guides everything we do, from the daily self-care rituals we inspire, to our procurement of local, organic, and sustainable products made by women, and our plastic-free policy.<br/><br/>Thanks to our integrated approach to wellness, gifting, and mindfulness, Tea and Tonic is a must-visit to enjoy tea, discover the finest sustainable products, and be nurtured in every way. We look forward to sharing a little tea with you, and we hope you feel nourished and inspired by every moment you spend with us at Tea & Tonic.<br/><br/>Love,<br/>Monni and the Tea and Tonic Team x</p>"
          }
        }
      },
